Restaurant liquor license application filed with the City Clerk’s office for Central Cafe,
LLC d/b/a Central Cafe, 3920 Central Avenue, Cheyenne, WY.   Dr. Rinne declared a conflict of
interest and vacated Council Chambers.  Mr. White moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Luna.
Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers.
Following announcement of the vote, Dr. Rinne returned to Council Chambers.

Announcement was made of a Public Hearing to be held Monday, August 27, 2018 at 6:00
p.m. in City Council Chambers, 2101 O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming, to determine whether
compliance of annexation conditions required by Wyoming Statute §15-1-402 exist for the S½
E½, Tract 1, Skyline Tracts, and that portion of Brimmer Road right-of-way adjacent to said S½
E½ of Tract 1, Laramie County, Wyoming, situated in SE¼ SE¼, Section 18, Township 14 North,
Range 66 West of the 6th P.M., County of Laramie, State of Wyoming  (located northwest of the
intersection of Storey Boulevard and Powderhouse Road).

Under other business:

Earl Janack shared his observations and concerns regarding the 2017 change to City Code
provisions involving street musicians and the requirement to obtain the consent of the owner or
manager of the premises in front of the place where a street musician proposes to perform.  Mr.
Janack commented on difficulties and scenarios he has encountered as a street performer; difficulty
in obtaining the required consent from owners or managers; available locations, and activities he
believes should require a City noise permit.  Mayor Orr suggested review of the City Code could
be conducted by the governing body with a separate meeting or response to Mr. Janack.
